      "time_created": 1789864864120,
      "time_updated": 1789864864122
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To complete the task, I need to create a Python script that extracts layout elements from a document using a concrete external provider. I will use the Amazon Textract service, which is a machine learning service that automatically extracts text and data from scanned documents. I will import the necessary AWS SDK for Python (Boto3) to interact with the Textract service. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864867377,
          "start": 1789864864123
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc42697b001yS3xlE7qOZo9wB",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc4262f7001ycQ341F2SV6uU5",
      "session_id": "ses_f43bd9d19ffeaUZqzVRuF9NoTj",
      "time_created": 1789864864123,
      "time_updated": 1789864867377
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_8RDUaGMAs3aKDzFHLFR9HT",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef extract_layout(document_path):\n    textract_client = boto3.client('textract')\n    \n    with open(document_path, 'rb') as document:\n        image_bytes = document.read()\n    \n    response = textract_client.analyze_document(\n        Document={'Bytes': image_bytes},\n        FeatureTypes=['TABLES', 'FORMS']\n    )\n    \n    blocks = response['Blocks']\n    \n    for block in blocks:\n        if block['BlockType'] == 'LINE':\n            print('LINE: ' + block['Text'])\n        elif block['BlockType'] == 'TABLE':\n            print('TABLE: ' + block['Text'])\n        \nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    document_path = 'sample_document.jpg'\n    extract_layout(document_path)",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-c2kcjku6/extract_layout.py"
          },
