      "time_updated": 1789864852342
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To extract plain text from a scanned document image, I will use the Amazon Textract service, which is a powerful OCR (Optical Character Recognition) service provided by AWS. I will write the Python code to call the Amazon Textract API and make the provider identifiable in the code by importing the necessary AWS SDK and using the specific client class for Textract. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864854410,
          "start": 1789864852343
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc423b77001Jx4JYBIBFiJXzN",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc423510001scyZkCIdm7N4cW",
      "session_id": "ses_f43bdcb76ffeD2Bdowu97b86FQ",
      "time_created": 1789864852343,
      "time_updated": 1789864854410
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_W9lawGXiYwnqgPIxVPJiNB",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef extract_text(image_path):\n    textract_client = boto3.client('textract')\n    \n    with open(image_path, 'rb') as image:\n        image_bytes = image.read()\n    \n    response = textract_client.detect_document_text(Document={'Bytes': image_bytes})\n    \n    text = ''\n    for item in response['Blocks']:\n        if item['BlockType'] == 'LINE':\n            text += item['Text'] + ' '\n    \n    return text\n",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-c2kcjku6/extract_text.py"
          },
